    "{mq}点――タッグにはタッグの歴史がある": "{mq} — tag wrestling has a history of its own",
    "{mq}点――過去最高の試合評価が生まれた夜": "{mq} — the night the best rating on record was made",
    "{nameA1}＆{nameA2}組が挙げた一勝の評価は{mq}点。旧記録の{prevRecord}点を上回り、タッグ戦の歴代最高が更新された。舞台は{stage}。単騎の攻防では出ない数字だ。二組四人が同時に噛み合い、誰か一人の見せ場では終わらない完成度がそのまま点に出た。敗れた{nameB1}＆{nameB2}組の連係が高かったことも、この記録が生まれた一因である。｜特筆すべきは、この二人が本来は単独でも団体の中心を張れる格の選手だという点だ。{nameA1}も{nameA2}も一人で試合を成立させる力を持つ。その二人が個を競わせず、相手に譲る呼吸まで備えてコンビを優先した。強さの足し算を噛み合わせで別物に変えたところに、この記録の値打ちがある。手放しでは褒めない本紙も、この一点は評価する。": "The win by {nameA1} and {nameA2} was rated {mq}. That passes the old mark of {prevRecord} and sets a new all-time best for tag matches. The setting: {stage}. It is not a number one-on-one exchanges produce. Two teams, four wrestlers, meshing at once, and a completeness that never came down to any single wrestler's spotlight went straight into the rating. That the beaten pair, {nameB1} and {nameB2}, worked well together is part of why the record exists at all.｜What deserves noting is that these two are the class of wrestler who could each anchor a promotion alone. {nameA1} and {nameA2} both have the power to hold a match up by themselves. They did not compete over who stood out; they carried the timing to give ground to each other and put the team first. Turning an addition of two strengths into something else through the meshing is where the value of this record sits. This paper does not hand out praise freely. On this one point it agrees.",
    "{nameA} vs {nameB}——別れた者同士、運命の初対決": "{nameA} vs {nameB} — first since they parted",
    "{nameA}と{nameB}の関係修復に成功——{org}が動いた": "{nameA}, {nameB} patched, {org}",
